<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Multimedia Player</title>

  <style>
    body {
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
      background-color: #111827;
      color: white;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 30px;
    }

    main {
      max-width: 800px;
      margin: auto;
    }

    h1 {
      text-align: center;
      color: #38bdf8;
    }

    section {
      background-color: #1f2937;
      padding: 25px;
      margin-bottom: 25px;
      border-radius: 12px;
    }

    h2 {
      color: #38bdf8;
    }

    audio, video {
      width: 100%;
      margin-top: 15px;
    }

    video {
      border-radius: 8px;
    }

    .transcript {
      line-height: 1.8;
      color: #d1d5db;
    }
  </style>
</head>

<body>

  <main>

    <h1>My Multimedia Player</h1>

    <!-- First Section: Audio Player -->
    <section>
      <h2>Now Playing: Sailing Away</h2>

      <audio controls aria-label="Sailing Away audio player">
        <source
          src="https://cdn.freecodecamp.org/curriculum/js-music-player/sailing-away.mp3"
          type="audio/mpeg">
      </audio>
    </section>

    <!-- Second Section: Video Player -->
    <section>
      <h2>Video: Understanding the Map Method</h2>

      <video
        controls
        width="600"
        aria-label="Video explaining how the JavaScript map method works">

        <source
          src="https://cdn.freecodecamp.org/curriculum/labs/what-is-the-map-method-and-how-does-it-work.mp4"
          type="video/mp4">

        <track
          src="https://cdn.freecodecamp.org/curriculum/labs/what-is-the-map-method-and-how-does-it-work.vtt"
          kind="subtitles"
          srclang="en"
          label="English">

      </video>
    </section>

    <!-- Third Section: Transcript -->
    <section>
      <h2>Video Transcript</h2>

      <p class="transcript">
        The JavaScript map method is used to create a new array
        by applying a function to every element in an existing array.
        It does not change the original array. Instead, it returns
        a new array containing the results of the function applied
        to each element.
      </p>
    </section>

  </main>

</body>
</html>

